<item><title>Wallis Lake Feral Deer Control Program</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> MidCoast Council (MCC) in cooperation with project partners including NSW Local Land Services has been undertaking ground shooting of Rusa deer (Cervus timorensis) to reduce the damage caused by expanding feral deer populations and to control the future expansion of feral deer into urban areas, including Forster and Old Bar. <br /><br />The Wallis Lake Feral Deer Program commenced in 2022 through a funding partnership with NSW Local Land Services and has continued in various forms since. The program initially used contractors for ground-shooting on Council-managed public land, but due to the cross-tenure nature of the program this has expanded to use of a boat to access islands and public foreshores, as well as ground-based shooting on private land with owner’s permission. During this time some 650 deer have been controlled over the combined target areas. NSW National Parks and Wildlife Service are also undertaking complementary ground shooting of Rusa deer in the target area on their land. <br /><br />As the...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> MidCoast Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 28/Aug/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP520286<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Farming & Animal Services & Equip<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 5]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=a2ebc0bbbc0e43d6a6b06bd013302258s520286se98f238c627243e7b15598cc3cf6cd26s1562</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">a2ebc0bbbc0e43d6a6b06bd013302258</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 05:04:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Farming &amp; Animal Services &amp; Equip</category>
</item>
<item><title>Fencing Works at Jack Pascoe Reserve Dog Park</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Central Goldfields Shire Council is seeking quotations for the fencing works associated with the Jack Pascoe Reserve Dog Park project, located at 1 Gartley Court, Maryborough.<br /><br />The project is funded by the Victorian Government through the Department of Energy, Environment and Climate Action (DEECA) under the New and Upgraded Dog Parks – Round 2 program, which forms part of the Open Space for Everyone Strategy 2021. The initiative supports the development and enhancement of accessible, inclusive, and high-quality public open spaces that promote community wellbeing, physical activity, and social connection.<br /><br />The Jack Pascoe Reserve Dog Park has been identified as a key community project to provide a safe and accessible off-leash area for residents and visitors. The project is being delivered by Central Goldfields Shire Council in partnership with DEECA as part of its commitment to improving community infrastructure and creating liveable, sustainable neighbourhoods.<br /><br />Further details...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Goldfields Shire Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 28/Aug/2026 03:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP520299<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
