<item><title>6245 - Robelle Domain Lagoon Desilt/Sediment Extraction</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Ipswich City Council is seeking to engage a suitably experienced and qualified Contractor to extract the accumulated sediment from Robelle Domain Lagoon and return to its as-designed state. Council's aim is to:<br /><br />- Reinstate the existing as-designed profile of the Lagoon<br /><br />- Ensuring the park infrastructure remains intact or, if modified/damaged, is returned to pre-project condition<br /><br />- Minimise disruptions to park operations and visitors usage.<br /><br />- Ensure all applicable minimum requirements for the exemption of a riverine protection permit are met, (Appropriate sediment control measure (E.g. silt curtains) are used to ensure disturbed sediment is not impacting water quality downstream of the lagoon.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> City of Ipswich<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 25/Aug/2026 11:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP519227<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Marine Transp. Products & Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 15]]></description>
