<category>Plant &amp; Equipment - Purchase</category>
</item>
<item><title>EOL Pumps Replacement – Pool Plantroom at MSAC</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The purpose of this project is to undertake the planned, like-for-like replacement of aging and end-of-life critical mechanical assets associated with pool water circulation and treatment systems. These assets are essential to maintaining safe, compliant, and continuous aquatic operations.<br /><br />The existing pumps and associated components have either reached or exceeded their operational lifecycle, exhibiting significant mechanical degradation and presenting a material risk of failure within a short timeframe. This project aims to eliminate these risks through proactive replacement and restore system reliability to acceptable operational <br /><br />standards.<br /><br />I.	4 x Outdoor Pool Circulation Pump Replacement<br /><br />II.	4 x Leisure Pool Feature Pump Replacement<br /><br />III.	1 x Hydrotherapy Pool Circulation Pump Replacement<br /><br />IV.	1 x Multipurpose HEX Booster Pump Replacement<br /><br />V.	7 x Sodium Hypochlorite Dosing Pump Replacement<br /><br />VI.	7 x Sodium Bisulphate Dosin...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> State Sport Centres Trust<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 19/Aug/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP517931<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Mechanical Plant, Equip, Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
